! A PROGRESSIVE VFL OPERATION THAT REFILLS ITS INDEX DOES ITS ARITHMETIC
! ONCE -- measured 2026-11-16 for docs/NEXT.md's G2.3 finding 3.
!
! The finding: binary +, +MG, * and *+ compute their result and write
! the accumulator on the execute() run that has the operand in hand,
! and a progressive operation whose index must be REFILLED then bails
! (the shared trailing block asks for the refill word) and runs again
! with both words in hand.  If the first run's accumulator write
! commits, the second run reads the NEW accumulator and the operation
! is applied twice: L is idempotent, + adds twice, * squares the
! multiplier's effect, *+ adds the product twice.
!
! THE MANUAL: Reference Manual 22-6530-2 printed p.21 (PDF 24),
! Progressive Indexing, Programming Notes, finished on printed p.22:
! "An operation in which progressive indexing is specified is executed
! in two parts.  The variable field length part of the operation is
! prepared and then the index modification portion of the operation is
! performed.  If an exception condition is detected during the variable
! field length portion of the operation, the entire operation will be
! suppressed ... However, if an exception condition is detected during
! the index modification portion of the operation, only this portion
! will be suppressed, the variable field length portion having been
! executed already."  So the arithmetic happens ONCE, then the index
! step (printed p.21: "For code 3, addition and counting take place and
! also the index specified by I is refilled if the count reaches
! zero").  V+ICR is code 3.
!
! EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS HAND-DERIVED from those pages and from the
! operations' own pages (ADD printed p.60, ADD TO MAGNITUDE p.60-61,
! MULTIPLY p.68 -- "the product of the addressed operand and the
! accumulator field specified by the offset is placed into the cleared
! accumulator at offset 20" -- MULTIPLY AND ADD p.69); none from a run.
! Each block loads index register 7 with XP1 (value OPND, count 1,
! refill RFW), so the count reaches zero and the index is refilled from
! RFW; the index word is stored after the operation (SX) to show the
! refill really happened -- without it the deck would not be looking at
! the path the finding is about.  The address part of each instruction
! is 0, so the value is not advanced before the refill replaces it.
!
!   P1  + :   acc 5, operand 3                 -> 8      (twice: 11)
!   P2  +MG:  acc 5, operand 3                 -> 8      (twice: 11)
!   P3  * :   acc 3, operand 5, offset 0        -> 15 at offset 20 =
!             (16)F00000  (twice: (16)F00000 * 5 at offset 20 =
!             (16)4B0000000000)
!   P4  *+:   factor 7 (LFT), acc 100, operand 5 -> 135  (twice: 170)
!   P5  L :   operand 3                         -> 3 (idempotent; the
!             control that L's refill path ends where it should)
!   P6  + with count 5 (no refill): acc 5 + 3  -> 8 (control: the same
!             add without the second run)
!   P7  / :   acc 100, operand 7, offset 0 -> quotient 14 in the
!             cleared accumulator (printed p.70: "the quotient is placed
!             in the cleared accumulator at the specified offset")
!             (twice: 14 / 7 = 2)
!   P8  C0110 (exclusive or, CONNECT, printed p.76: "The result replaces
!             the accumulator field"): acc 5, operand 3 -> 6 (twice: 5)
!   Rk  the index word after Pk: RFW's contents for P1-P5, P7, P8; for P6, the
!       count down to 4, value and refill unchanged.
!
! MEASURED 2026-11-16 ON THE UNMODIFIED MODEL (batch9 + this deck), the
! finding confirmed: FAILS P1_add 11, P2_addmg 11, P3_mul (16)4B0000000000,
! P4_muladd 170, P7_div 2, P8_xor 5 -- exactly the "twice" values above;
! P5, P6 and every Rk pass (the refill happened, once).  Fixed by
! vflRefillOutstanding (StretchExecute.bsv).
!
! INJECTION, observed: the guard removed from the binary + / +MG arm only
! (the "end else if (!isValid(needsRead) && !vflRefillOutstanding(...))"
! line back to "!isValid(needsRead)"): FAILS P1_add 11 and P2_addmg 11,
! nothing else here; vfl_decimal_add and vfl_binary_add_indicators stay
! green.  Reverted from the saved copy, checked with cmp.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   L(BU,64,8), FIVE
        LX,  $X7, XP1
        +(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P1
        SX,  $X7, R1
        L(BU,64,8), FIVE
        LX,  $X7, XP1
        +MG(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P2
        SX,  $X7, R2
        L(BU,64,8), THREE
        LX,  $X7, XP1F
        *(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P3
        SX,  $X7, R3
        LFT(BU,64), SEVEN
        L(BU,64,8), HUND
        LX,  $X7, XP1F
        *+(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P4
        SX,  $X7, R4
        L(BU,64,8), FIVE
        LX,  $X7, XP1
        L(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P5
        SX,  $X7, R5
        L(BU,64,8), FIVE
        LX,  $X7, XP5
        +(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P6
        SX,  $X7, R6
        L(BU,64,8), HUND
        LX,  $X7, XP1S
        /(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P7
        SX,  $X7, R7
        L(BU,64,8), FIVE
        LX,  $X7, XP1
        C0110(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        ST(BU,64,8), P8
        SX,  $X7, R8
PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, 1500.0
XP1     XW, OPND, 1, RFW         ! count 1: the refill fires
XP1F    XW, OPNDF, 1, RFW
XP5     XW, OPND, 5, RFW         ! count 5: no refill
XP1S    XW, SEVEN, 1, RFW
RFW     XW, 1234.0, 77, 1500.0   ! the refilled index word
OPND    DD(BU,64,8), 3
OPNDF   DD(BU,64,8), 5
THREE   DD(BU,64,8), 3
FIVE    DD(BU,64,8), 5
SEVEN   DD(BU,64,8), 7
HUND    DD(BU,64,8), 100

        SLC, 1700.0
P1      DD(BU,64), 0
P2      DD(BU,64), 0
P3      DD(BU,64), 0
P4      DD(BU,64), 0
P5      DD(BU,64), 0
P6      DD(BU,64), 0
R1      DD(BU,64), 0
R2      DD(BU,64), 0
R3      DD(BU,64), 0
R4      DD(BU,64), 0
R5      DD(BU,64), 0
R6      DD(BU,64), 0
P7      DD(BU,64), 0
R7      DD(BU,64), 0
P8      DD(BU,64), 0
R8      DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
